# AIFS-RAPS Direct Container

This folder builds one self-contained AIFS-RAPS benchmark image. The image
contains the Python environment, Anemoi packages, configs, grids, and generated
dummy Zarr datasets under `/data`.

Users do not need this repo to run the image. They need the image reference, a
writable mount for `/work` to retain outputs, and a writable mount for `/graphs`
to retain generated graph files.

## Build

```bash
IMAGE=...

docker build \
  --build-arg BASE_IMAGE=nvcr.io/nvidia/pyg:26.01-py3 \
  --build-arg ANEMOI_BRANCH=aifs-raps_20251215 \
  -t "$IMAGE" .
```

Push `$IMAGE` to GitLab or another registry that Enroot/Pyxis can pull.

## Run

The image provides one command:

```bash
aifs-benchmark throughput
aifs-benchmark highres
aifs-benchmark throughput-generate-graph
aifs-benchmark highres-generate-graph
aifs-benchmark correctness
aifs-benchmark smoke
```

Example SLURM usage without any launcher checkout:

```bash
srun \
  -N 1 \
  -n 4 \
  --mpi=pmix \
  --container-image=<image-ref> \
  --container-mounts "$PWD:/work,$PWD/graphs:/graphs" \
  --container-workdir=/work \
  aifs-benchmark throughput
```

Runtime overrides are environment variables, for example:

```bash
batch_limit=45 max_epochs=2 num_workers=2 run_prefix=test \
srun ... aifs-benchmark throughput
```

The benchmark commands expect a SLURM allocation and derive node count from
`SLURM_NNODES`. Each node is assumed to have four GPUs.

Generate each graph once, then reuse it for normal runs:

```bash
mkdir -p graphs
srun ... aifs-benchmark throughput-generate-graph
srun ... aifs-benchmark throughput
```

Both commands use `/graphs` inside the container.

The correctness benchmark uses the real O48 dataset rather than a generated
dummy dataset. Mount the dataset parent at `/data/correctness`:

```bash
srun \
  -N 1 \
  -n 4 \
  --mpi=pmix \
  --container-image=<image-ref> \
  --container-mounts "$PWD:/work,$PWD/graphs:/graphs,/path/to/dataset-parent:/data/correctness:ro" \
  --container-workdir=/work \
  aifs-benchmark correctness
```

By default it expects:

```text
/data/correctness/aifs-ea-an-oper-0001-mars-o48-1979-2022-6h-v6.zarr
```

If the mounted dataset has another name, set `correctness_dataset` to the
directory name inside `/data/correctness`.

The thin `*.slurm` files one directory up are examples for Lyris allocations:

```bash
cd ..
sbatch throughput.slurm
sbatch high-res.slurm
sbatch --export=ALL,correctness_data_host=/path/to/dataset.zarr correctness.slurm
```

## Editable `anemoi-core`

Mount a local checkout at `/opt/anemoi-core`:

```bash
srun \
  --container-image=<image-ref> \
  --container-mounts "$PWD:/work,$PWD/graphs:/graphs,/path/to/anemoi-core:/opt/anemoi-core" \
  --container-workdir=/work \
  aifs-benchmark throughput
```

`aifs-benchmark` detects component `src` directories under the mounted checkout
and prepends them to `PYTHONPATH`, so code changes can be tested without
rebuilding the image.

The SLURM wrappers expose the same mount as `anemoi_core_host`:

```bash
sbatch --export=ALL,anemoi_core_host=/path/to/anemoi-core throughput.slurm
```
